@startuml
!include ../common/style.puml

title HANBAY HOTEL - Current Deployment Architecture

top to bottom direction

actor "User" as User

node "Developer Machine" as DeveloperMachine {

    node "Web Browser" as Browser {
        artifact "HANBAY HOTEL UI\nReact 19 + TypeScript" as WebUI
    }

    node "Node.js Runtime" as NodeRuntime {
        component "Vite Development Server" as ViteServer
        artifact "client/" as FrontendSource
    }

    node "Java 17 Runtime" as JavaRuntime {
        component "Spring Boot Application\nhotel-management" as BackendApp
        artifact "hotel-booking-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar" as BackendJar

        component "Actuator" as Actuator
        component "Spring Data JPA" as Jpa
        component "Flyway" as Flyway
        component "Spring Security" as Security
    }

    node "Docker Engine" as DockerEngine {
        component "Docker Compose" as DockerCompose

        database "PostgreSQL Container\npostgres:latest" as LocalPostgres {
            artifact "Hotel Management Database" as LocalDatabase
        }
    }
}

cloud "GitHub" as GitHub {

    artifact "Source Repository" as Repository

    node "GitHub Actions" as GitHubActions {

        node "Frontend CI\nUbuntu + Node.js 22" as FrontendCI {
            component "npm ci" as NpmInstall
            component "Prettier Check" as PrettierCheck
            component "ESLint" as EslintCheck
            component "Vitest" as FrontendTest
            component "TypeScript + Vite Build" as FrontendBuild
        }

        node "Backend CI\nUbuntu + Java 17" as BackendCI {
            component "Maven Verify" as MavenVerify

            database "PostgreSQL 17\nTest Service" as TestPostgres {
                artifact "hotel_test_db" as TestDatabase
            }
        }
    }
}

' ===== Local runtime connections =====

User --> Browser : Access web application

FrontendSource --> ViteServer : Loaded and bundled
ViteServer --> WebUI : Serves frontend assets
Browser --> ViteServer : HTTP\nVite development port

WebUI --> BackendApp : REST API over HTTP\nBase URL from VITE_API_BASE_URL

BackendJar --> BackendApp : Executed by Java 17

BackendApp --> Security : Authenticate and authorize requests
BackendApp --> Actuator : Expose health and info endpoints
BackendApp --> Jpa : Persist and query domain data
BackendApp --> Flyway : Run database migrations on startup

Jpa --> LocalPostgres : JDBC
Flyway --> LocalPostgres : Schema migration

DockerCompose --> LocalPostgres : Create and manage container
BackendApp --> DockerCompose : Spring Boot Docker Compose support

' ===== CI connections =====

Repository --> GitHubActions : Push or pull request

FrontendCI --> NpmInstall
NpmInstall --> PrettierCheck
PrettierCheck --> EslintCheck
EslintCheck --> FrontendTest
FrontendTest --> FrontendBuild

BackendCI --> MavenVerify
MavenVerify --> TestPostgres : JDBC\nlocalhost:5432
MavenVerify --> MavenVerify : Compile, format check\nand automated tests

note right of WebUI
Runtime configuration:

VITE_API_BASE_URL is required.
VITE_APP_NAME is optional.
end note

note right of BackendApp
Default application configuration:

Application: hotel-management
Profile: local
Server port: 8080
Health: /actuator/health
Info: /actuator/info
end note

note right of LocalPostgres
compose.yaml currently defines:

POSTGRES_DB=mydatabase
POSTGRES_USER=myuser
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=secret

The host port is dynamically assigned
because compose.yaml specifies "5432"
without a fixed host port.
end note

note bottom of LocalPostgres
When Spring Boot Docker Compose support starts PostgreSQL,
it discovers the container connection automatically.

When PostgreSQL is started manually, the local profile uses:

DB_URL=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/hotel_management
DB_USERNAME=hotel
DB_PASSWORD=hotel
end note

note bottom of GitHubActions
Frontend CI runs when files under client/ change.

Backend CI runs when files under hotel-booking/ change.

The current workflows verify the source code.
They do not deploy the application to production.
end note

legend left
|= Element |= Current responsibility |
| Browser | Runs the React frontend |
| Vite | Serves frontend during local development |
| Spring Boot | Hosts REST API and application logic |
| PostgreSQL | Stores persistent business data |
| Docker Compose | Provides local PostgreSQL |
| GitHub Actions | Runs frontend and backend verification |
endlegend

@enduml